{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And the children of Israel journeyed from Beeroth Bene-jaakan to Moserah; there Aaron died. The death of Aaron is juxtaposed next to the breaking of the tablets, to teach you that the death of the righteous is as difficult as the breaking of the tablets. And also a Torah scholar who died — everyone becomes his relative, who must tear [keriah] over him as over a Torah scroll that was burned. And further, 'and I placed the tablets in the ark' is juxtaposed next to the death of Aaron, to teach: a Torah scroll that wore out is buried next to a Torah scholar — to say: this one fulfilled what is written in that one." "<b>And he buried</b> — ויכהן. The death of the righteous atones like the priestly garments."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:19.183797732Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}